WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.605
The evaluation is deliberately broad.

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:04.129
For structural shift,

00:00:04.209 --> 00:00:12.257
the authors build a Rotated Super-pixel MNIST
benchmark where increasing rotation induces controlled distortion.

00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:18.208
For size shift, they use standard graph
classification datasets including D and D,

00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:22.562
NCI1, NCI109, and PROTEINS with GCN, GIN, and PNA
backbones.

00:00:22.642 --> 00:00:24.957
For concept and covariate shifts,

00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:30.980
they use the GOOD benchmark suite covering colored
MNIST, motif, and SST2 datasets.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:37.874
Across all of these they compare against strong
uncertainty baselines including deep ensembles,

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:43.244
temperature scaling, and Monte Carlo dropout,
measuring calibration error,

00:00:43.324 --> 00:00:49.050
out-of-distribution detection AUROC, and
generalization gap mean absolute error.
